---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Download">
	<section class="py-24 sm:py-32">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
			<h2 class="text-base font-semibold leading-7 text-ctp-mauve uppercase tracking-wider">Get Started</h2>
			<h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ctp-text sm:text-6xl">
				Download the client.
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-6 mx-auto max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-ctp-subtext1">
				Decentralized communication is ready for your community. 
				Binaries for all platforms are coming soon.
			</p>

			<div class="mx-auto mt-20 max-w-2xl">
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
					<div class="rounded-2xl border border-ctp-surface1 bg-ctp-mantle p-8 text-center shadow-xl">
						<div class="text-4xl mb-4">🐧 / 🪟 / 🍎</div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ctp-text">Standard Downloads</h3>
						<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ctp-subtext0">Coming soon for Windows, Linux, and macOS.</p>
						<div class="mt-6 inline-block w-full py-2 bg-ctp-surface1 text-ctp-subtext1 rounded font-semibold opacity-50 cursor-not-allowed">
							Coming Soon
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="rounded-2xl border border-ctp-mauve bg-ctp-mantle p-8 text-center shadow-xl">
						<div class="text-4xl mb-4">⚙️</div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ctp-text">Build from Source</h3>
						<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ctp-subtext0">Developer-focused: build the client locally with Rust and Node.js.</p>
						<a href="https://github.com/icub3d/decentcom#building-from-source" class="mt-6 inline-block w-full py-2 bg-ctp-mauve text-ctp-crust rounded font-semibold hover:bg-ctp-mauve/90 transition">
							View Guide
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="mx-auto mt-24 max-w-2xl text-left border-t border-ctp-surface1 pt-16">
				<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ctp-text mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
				<dl class="space-y-8">
					<div>
						<dt class="text-lg font-semibold text-ctp-text">Is there a web client?</dt>
						<dd class="mt-2 text-ctp-subtext1">Currently, decentcom is focused on a desktop application for better security (private keys are stored in the OS keychain and signing happens in the Rust core, not the browser).</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt class="text-lg font-semibold text-ctp-text">How do I host my own server?</dt>
						<dd class="mt-2 text-ctp-subtext1">A server can be run as a single binary or a Docker container. Check the <a href="https://github.com/icub3d/decentcom/tree/main/server" class="text-ctp-mauve hover:underline">server documentation</a> for instructions.</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
